  "term": "ethnic group",
  "definition": "An ethnic group is a social group whose members share a distinctive cultural and social tradition that is passed across generations. People in the group typically share a common history, origin, identity, and similar life experiences or habits, and may also share genetic heritage that can shape patterns of health and disease.",
